                <SliderW tabIndex="1" initialValue="7" />
              </VStack>
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

        <!-- === aria-label: accessible name and test automation === -->
        <Card>
          <H2>
            aria-label — accessible names for automation
          </H2>
          <Markdown>
            <![CDATA[
The trace-tools pipeline locates elements by aria role and name. Both sliders below
set `aria-label="Volume"`. Click **Query DOM** to run
`querySelector('[aria-label="Volume"]')` against each — Playwright's
`getByRole('slider', { name: 'Volume' })` does the same thing under the hood.
]]>
          </Markdown>
          <HStack>
            <VStack width="50%">
              <Text fontWeight="bold">
                Slider (aria-label — ignored)
              </Text>
              <Slider
                aria-label="Volume"
                minValue="0"
                maxValue="100"
                initialValue="50" />
            </VStack>
            <SpaceFiller />
            <VStack width="50%">
              <Text fontWeight="bold">
                SliderW (aria-label — works)
              </Text>
              <SliderW
                aria-label="Volume"
                minValue="0"
                maxValue="100"
                initialValue="50" />
            </VStack>
          </HStack>
          <Markdown>
            <![CDATA[
**Expected result:** `querySelectorAll('[aria-label="Volume"]')` finds **1 match** (SliderW only).
If both wrappers forwarded the attribute, it would find **2 matches**.
]]>
          </Markdown>
        </Card>

      </VStack>
    </Page>

    <Page url="/knob">
      <VStack padding="2rem" gap="2rem">

        <H1>
          Knob
        </H1>

        <Markdown>
          <![CDATA[
**Knob** wraps [react-knob-headless](https://github.com/satelllte/react-knob-headless) — an unstyled, accessible knob primitive. It's not Radix. It's not even the same API shape. But `wrapCompound` doesn't care: it handles the XMLUI state lifecycle (`initialValue`, `updateState`, `didChange`, component APIs) for any React component that takes `value` and `onChange`.

The render component (**KnobRender.tsx**) is ~80 lines of pure React. The wrapCompound config (**KnobWrapped.tsx**) is ~30 lines. No hand-written renderer, no XMLUI imports in the render component.

Drag up/down on the knob to change the value, or use the buttons below.
]]>
        </Markdown>

        <Card var.knobVal="">
          <H2>
            Basic: 0–100
          </H2>
          <HStack alignItems="center" gap="2rem">
            <Knob
              id="k1"
              minValue="0"
              maxValue="100"
              step="1"
              initialValue="50"
              onDidChange="{(v) => knobVal = v}" />
            <Text>
              Value: {knobVal}
            </Text>
          </HStack>
          <HStack>
            <Button onClick="{k1.setValue(0)}">
              Set 0
            </Button>
            <Button onClick="{k1.setValue(50)}">
              Set 50
            </Button>
            <Button onClick="{k1.setValue(100)}">
              Set 100
            </Button>
          </HStack>
        </Card>

        <Card var.knobVal2="">
